   Toolchains — the tools kit runs on, and what installs them

   ✅ bash 5.2 runs kit
   ❌ jq is not installed
      brew install jq
   ❌ several tool managers are usable for the project: mise, brew; choose one
      kit toolchains use mise
      or: kit toolchains use brew
   ❌ brew is installed but not on PATH
      eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"
      add it to your shell profile to keep it

   kit runs on four tools: bash, git, jq, and yq. This step checks each one.
   Then it checks the machine's package manager, such as brew or apt, which
   installs them.

   When a check fails, the line under it gives the command that fixes it, or
   says where to read more. Run the command yourself, or have kit run it and
